					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13884347#post-4830048</guid>
				<title>Individual Rating Modules for Log Entries: Tech Staff Post - Info</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13884347/individual-rating-modules-for-log-entries#post-4830048</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2020 07:30:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Nagiros</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>4665703</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>I thought that the log of extranormal events or unexplained locations was already like this, but it seems that I was mistaken.</p> </blockquote> <p>It was the Unexplained Locations log; the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2673-containment-maintenance-log">SCP-2673 Containment Maintenance Log</a> also previously had the system you're describing. These logs were intentionally reverted back to their module-less form because the way in which individual modules are achieved is fairly complex, tends to create lots of near-contentless pages, and is ultimately more of a pain to manage than just pruning the logs themselves.</p> <p>The decision to go back to the old way of things was deliberate and we don't intend to reverse that decision any time soon. Thank you for your interest in improving the site, however.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13884347#post-4830022</guid>
				<title>Individual Rating Modules for Log Entries: Individual Rating Modules for Log Entries</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13884347/individual-rating-modules-for-log-entries#post-4830022</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2020 06:51:06 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Kothardarastrix</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3460794</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Low-quality content naturally piles up in places like 682's termination log, 1459's extended logs, and other very large collaborative lists. Inevitably, a page curator has to go through and prune away the bad entries. I imagine that this is tiresome and time-consuming for the curator, and it also means that garbage entries in these logs live much longer than an equally garbage SCP would. If there were some way to install individual rating modules for each item on the log, so they could be voted on individually, then perhaps that might save some time for the curator and shorten the lifespan of the bad entries.</p> <p>I thought that the log of extranormal events or unexplained locations was already like this, but it seems that I was mistaken.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
