					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13260150#post-4829610</guid>
				<title>Tag Thread 3: Revenge of the Tags: Re: Tag Request - porcine</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13260150/tag-thread-3:revenge-of-the-tags#post-4829610</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2020 19:27:59 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Nagiros</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>4665703</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Denied.</p> <p>Hey, thanks for requesting. Attribute tags have a higher expectation of applicable articles in order to be considered, and <em>we expect lists of applicable articles to be mostly, if not totally, complete upon posting</em>. Moreover, attribute tags are not applied to GOI formats, and the tech team is very hesitant to approval more animal tags due to how many we have already.</p> <p>Additionally, for yourself and for others interested in proposing future tags: <strong>please do not collapse your own posts</strong>. We do that ourselves after the decision is made to tidy up the thread, and doing that beforehand just makes your post difficult to spot.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
