					<![CDATA[
						 <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;porcine&nbsp;==&nbsp;DENIED</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;porcine&nbsp;==&nbsp;DENIED</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p>We've already got all sorts of animal tags like bovine and leoporine, but somehow we don't have one for the most horrifying animals of all. Tag would be applied to SCP documents and GOI formats describing pigs and pig-related phenomena.</p> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4446">SCP-4446</a> by BlueSentinel</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-509">SCP-509</a> by Anaxagoras</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/adoption-poster-pearl">Adoption Poster: Pearl</a> by Rounderhouse</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4381">SCP-4381</a> by Kenoma</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2779">SCP-2779</a> by Rimple</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4495">SCP-4495</a> and <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5994">SCP-5994</a> by UraniumEmpire</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5740">SCP-5740</a> by djkaktus</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2727">SCP-2727</a> by Flower on the Wall</li> </ul> <p>And probably many more, but I'm only on page 2 of a search for &quot;pig&quot; and that's already 9 x 8.</p> </div> </div> </div> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
